<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR falls on cue from call money.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR falls on cue from call money.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) slipped across all maturities following the weakness in the overnight and termed peso rates, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The PHIBOR are just reflecting the movement in the peso rates,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Overnight and termed rates went down after the Central Bank limited its overnight borrowing and kept its termed reverse repo windows close.</p>
<p>Banks were left with no other options but to swamp the secondary Treasury bills market.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 AUG 30		  AUG 29</p>
<p>    1 W		10 15/16		11 1/8</p>
<p>    2 W		11			11 1/8</p>
<p>    1 M		11			11 1/4</p>
<p>    2 M		11			11 5/16</p>
<p>    3 M		11  1/16		11 5/16</p>
<p>    6 M		11  3/8		 11 9/16</p>
<p>    12M		11 13/16		11 15/16</p>
<p>    VAL		2-Sep		   30-Aug</p>
